1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
How many hours of revision is enough?

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,200
mark = m × hours + b

3
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,400
Four students. Hours revised, and the mark they got.

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:10,400
48, 52, 60, 72. No straight line goes through all four.

5
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,600
So take the line that misses least. Every miss is 2, total 16.

6
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:17,200
One more hour is worth 8 marks. That is m.

7
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,800
With zero hours it starts at 38. That is b.

8
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:24,000
So what if you do five?

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,200
8 × 5 + 38 = 78.

10
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,600
And now the part nobody says out loud.

11
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:31,200
The line knows four people. It does not know you.

12
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:32,800
Every AI has this problem: it learns a pattern, then gets asked about someone new.

13
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,000
We learned this at school.

14
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,200
Nobody ever said what for.

15
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,800
Send this to your school friend — and tell them THIS is how it's solved.

16
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:40,000
Follow for the math behind AI. @observer.collapse
